# .codebase-map.conf — per-repo config for the codebase-map kit.
# Copy to your repo ROOT as `.codebase-map.conf` and edit. RESTRICTED grammar — the same file
# is sourced by bash AND parsed by map_lib.load_conf(): plain KEY=VALUE assignments; a value
# with spaces MUST be double-quoted; no inline comments after a value; no `export`. Commit it
# LF (add `.codebase-map.conf text eol=lf` to .gitattributes) — a CRLF-checked-out conf
# leaves stray carriage returns in bash-sourced values on Linux.
# The kit dir itself is copied in as a directory NAMED `codebase-map` (a fixed convention the
# gate template resolves the kit by — do not rename it). Its PREFIX under the repo root is free:
# `<root>/codebase-map/` and `<root>/<prefix>/codebase-map/` both work. THIS FILE is the marker that
# says where the root is — the kit walks up from its own directory looking for it — so it belongs
# at the repo ROOT and nowhere else, whatever prefix the kit sits at.

# Root of the map tree, relative to the repo root. If the memory-tree kit is adopted, put it
# under that tree (e.g. memory/map) so its hygiene gate covers the prose files; otherwise
# docs/map works fine.
MAP_ROOT=memory/map

# Where adopt-codebase-map.sh copies the gate template — a path INSIDE the directory your
# project's existing test suite collects (pytest/vitest-adjacent/…). Zero CI changes by
# design: the gate rides the suite that already gates your merge bar.
GATE_FILE=tests/test_codebase_map.py

# The digest command, verbatim — consumed by the scaffolded map README and the kickoff
# manifest (humans/docs; gate remedy messages derive their own spelling from the install prefix).
# adopt-codebase-map.sh STAMPS this line with the kit's real prefix when it creates the conf, so
# the value below is only the shape. Adjust if your launcher differs — `uv run python …`,
# `python3 …` — and keep the path pointing at the kit dir you actually installed.
MAP_DIFF_CMD="python <prefix>/codebase-map/map_diff.py"   # the pre-stamp shape; adopt-codebase-map.sh rewrites this line per prefix

# --- reuse-convergence layer (optional; only meaningful with the SYMBOL recall tier) ----------

# Layers you deliberately do NOT cover with a SYMBOL_EXTRACTOR (map_extractors.py) — a
# space/comma-separated list of FILE EXTENSIONS, each with its leading dot: ".sh .ts". Language
# NAMES are the old spelling and are REFUSED, not reinterpreted: reading `bash` as `.sh` is right
# once and wrong for `c` or `go`, and an adopter carrying the old value has to be told rather than
# guessed at.
#
# You do not have to author this from memory. The set is DERIVED from the corpus walk, so a layer
# that is present, has no extractor and is not listed here makes `reuse_lookup.py` REFUSE and name
# the extension and its file count. Run it once and paste back the layers you meant to leave dark.
# Leave empty when every present layer has an extractor. Quote it — it has spaces.
RECALL_DARK_LAYERS=""

# Fan-in + install sites at/above which a symbol counts as a reusable "seam": files referencing it
# (import/identifier positions) plus files carrying an inlined canonical copy of it (a `# >>> <name>`
# marker). Used by reuse_lookup and gen_map --seed-affordances alike. Integer >= 1;
# default 3. Raise it in a big repo where 3 files is common, lower it in a small one.
SEAM_FANIN_THRESHOLD=3

# How many feature dossiers may declare an EMPTY `decisions` list. SHRINK-ONLY: it is a debt
# being drained, not a tolerance. SHIPS UNSET ON PURPOSE — a number measured on gov's corpus is
# either vacuous or permanently red on yours. Unset, the check reports the count as UNGRADED and
# says so rather than reading it as zero (which would red your first run) or skipping silently
# (which would make the check the vacuous selector it exists to close). Measure yours, then set
# it, and record the reading beside it. Enforcement of the shrink-only half needs the
# drift-audit kit, whose RATCHETS list reds an unjustified raise; without that kit the pin is a
# declared number with no gate behind it, which is a documented gap rather than a silent one.
DOSSIER_DECISIONS_EMPTY_PIN=""
